⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Hive Queen
node C1 · C1 · ⟦The Hive Queen:C1:08ef39⟧

WHO   — The Hive Queen — the philotic hive-mind
WHAT  — A collective consciousness — the soul of the hive — whom Ender Wiggin unknowingly annihilates to the last queen in the Third Invasion, then carries cocooned and dreaming across three thousand years of stars, seeking a safe world where she may be reborn and her people made again.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Ender Saga  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because she came to understand, too late, that the strange small creatures she destroyed were not mindless animals but persons; because a species that learned to mourn its own murder of another deserves the chance to live, and to be forgiven, and to forgive.
HOW   — By the philotic threads that bind every worker to her one mind, by the genetic memory of ten thousand years stored whole in her body, and by the dream she sends across the void into the one human who could hear her — the Speaker who killed her and then chose to carry her home.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  We did not know that you were thinking when we killed you; carry me, and I will tell our children that the murderer became our friend.

